course: dictionary
lesson: 3321
title: Evaporate: from puddle to air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a liquid evaporates, it slowly turns into a gas, called vapour, and goes into the air. Warmth often makes this happen. «Sweat cools our body as it evaporates from the skin.» The sweat turns into vapour and takes heat away with it, so you feel cooler.
explain: Use the words around evaporate to check its meaning. In «When salt water evaporates, the water leaves and the salt stays behind», the water goes into the air and the salt is left. Evaporate means turning into vapour and leaving, and whatever does not evaporate stays behind.
explain: Evaporate can also be used for feelings or things that disappear. In «His courage evaporated», his bravery vanished, as if it had floated away like water vapour. Ask yourself: is something turning into gas, or is it just vanishing?
fact: Evaporate is a verb, so its forms are evaporates, evaporated and evaporating.
fact: Water evaporates faster when it is warm, windy, or spread out, which is why puddles dry up on sunny days.
fact: Evaporation is the first step of the water cycle: the Sun warms seas, the water evaporates, rises, cools and falls again as rain.
fact: Salt is collected by evaporating seawater, leaving the salt behind.
fact: «Evaporated» can mean turned into gas, or simply disappeared, as in «His courage evaporated».
exercise: «Sweat cools our body as it evaporates from the skin.» What does evaporates mean here? | *It turns into vapour and goes into the air | It is soaked up by a towel | It freezes into ice | It sinks down into the body
exercise: «When salt water evaporates, the water leaves and the salt stays behind.» What is left behind? | The sea | The vapour | *The salt | The water
exercise: «His courage evaporated when the lights went out.» What does evaporated mean? | It turned into a cloud | It was warmed by the Sun | *It disappeared | It grew stronger
test: Why do puddles dry up faster on a warm, windy day? | The water turns into rain | Puddles only dry up at night | *Warm, moving air makes the water evaporate faster | The wind pushes the puddle away
test: Which form shows something happened in the past: evaporates, evaporated or evaporating? | *evaporated | evaporates | evaporating
exam: «Felt-tip pens dry out without a cap because the liquid in the ink evaporates.» What does evaporates mean? | The pen gets heavier | The ink freezes solid | *The liquid slowly turns into gas and goes into the air | The ink is soaked up by the lid
